  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Your Website Title Studios Journal Jobs Submit Overview Buy Carbon Studios Journal Jobs Submit Overview Buy Carbon Inside Studio Ombra: three portfolios, one rule Giulia Romano on designing portfolios for photographers who would rather you never noticed the website. Type Interview Published 2 Oct 2026 The site in this story Semplice by Studio Ombra Studio Ombra has designed portfolios for photographers, architects and a model agency, and all three are in the directory: Semplice, Riflesso and Studiomax. Giulia Romano runs the studio with Matteo Conti. What is the one rule? Nothing on the page can be more interesting than the pictures. No hover effects that move images, no cursors, no loaders. If a photographer sends a client a link, the client should see work in under a second. Semplice is almost empty. Was that hard to sell? Not to the photographer. She wanted a clock, her name and her work. The clock was her idea: she shoots for magazines in different time zones, and it tells editors when she is awake. How do you handle hundreds of images? Riflesso is the extreme case. We treat every project like a contact sheet: strict columns, small captions and big margins. The ",
